  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Good, Decent Toilets for 49 families in Zimbabwe</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In the Matopos region of Zimbabwe, local volunteers identified 49 families infected or affected with HIV/AIDS who lack a toilet. This means that these families are defecating and urinating in the tall grasses or forests surrounding their homes. AFCA will build long drop toilets (loos) using recycled materials, providing the families with decent and safe toilets. A solar lamp will complete the package, allowing beneficiaries to use the facilities with the aid of a light.</narrative>
  </description>
